WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.099
The Evaluate phase asks whether the course worked and how it should improve.

00:00:05.099 --> 00:00:07.407
Evaluation happens in two broad ways.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:10.098
Formative evaluation occurs during design and development,

00:00:10.098 --> 00:00:14.329
when feedback can still shape the course before or during rollout.

00:00:14.329 --> 00:00:18.943
Summative evaluation occurs after delivery, when the team looks at course results,

00:00:18.943 --> 00:00:20.866
learner outcomes, and improvement opportunities.

00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:24.712
Formative evaluation can include storyboard reviews, prototype reviews, accessibility checks,

00:00:24.712 --> 00:00:28.557
usability tests, pilot feedback, SME feedback, and early learner observations.

00:00:28.557 --> 00:00:33.556
The purpose is to improve the course before the full audience experiences it.

00:00:33.556 --> 00:00:36.248
A confusing interaction, weak example, poor caption,

00:00:36.248 --> 00:00:42.401
or mismatched quiz question is much easier to fix before launch than after a compliance deadline.

00:00:42.401 --> 00:00:44.708
Summative evaluation uses evidence after delivery.

00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:48.939
Common signals include learner feedback, quiz results, completion data, LMS reports,

00:00:48.939 --> 00:00:52.015
support tickets, manager feedback, performance indicators, quality metrics,

00:00:52.015 --> 00:00:53.169
and workplace observation.

00:00:53.169 --> 00:00:54.707
Each signal has limits.

00:00:54.707 --> 00:00:57.399
Completion data tells you whether learners finished,

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:00.091
but not necessarily whether they can perform.

00:01:00.091 --> 00:01:03.936
Quiz results may show recall, but not always workplace transfer.

00:01:03.936 --> 00:01:06.628
Useful evaluation looks beyond attendance and completion.

00:01:06.628 --> 00:01:11.243
If the course was meant to reduce errors, improve decisions, support compliance,

00:01:11.243 --> 00:01:15.473
or standardize a process, look for evidence connected to that outcome.

00:01:15.473 --> 00:01:18.549
Sometimes the evidence shows the course needs revision.

00:01:18.549 --> 00:01:23.933
Sometimes it shows the course is fine but the job environment needs better tools,

00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:25.856
clearer policies, or manager reinforcement.

00:01:25.856 --> 00:01:28.163
Evaluation should feed the next iteration.

00:01:28.163 --> 00:01:32.778
Capture what worked, what confused learners, what reviewers flagged, what data changed,

00:01:32.778 --> 00:01:34.701
and what updates are needed.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:38.931
ADDIE becomes a cycle when evaluation informs future analysis, design, development,

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:39.700
and implementation.
